// Declaration generation for the repo's plain-JS `.mjs` modules that TypeScript
// files import (WI-6394).
//
// A `.mjs` with no sibling `.d.mts` costs every TS importer a TS7016 ("implicitly
// has an 'any' type"), which then gets absorbed into that file's permanent
// per-file tsc baseline — where it silently tolerates the NEXT real error in the
// same file. That is the whole reason this exists.
//
// WHY GENERATED RATHER THAN HAND-WRITTEN. The repo's earlier convention was a
// hand-maintained sibling `.d.mts` (see `scripts/lint-tsc.d.mts`). That file has
// drifted from its `.mjs` twice — `parseExplicitFiles`, then
// `formatAttributionHeadline` — and each drift made the missing export a TS2305
// for every importer and cost that file a permanent baselined error. It now needs
// its own hand-written drift test to police it. A hand-synced projection of a
// source it cannot see change is the defect; adding more of them scales the
// defect. Generating from the source removes the class instead.
//
// Even with NO JSDoc the emit is worth having: tsc still infers every return type
// and const literal from the implementation, so only undocumented parameters land
// as `any` — a strict improvement on the entire module being `any`.
//
// ADDING A MODULE: append it to `files` below, run `npm run gen:declarations`, and
// commit the emitted `.d.mts` beside it. `npm run gen:declarations:check` (and the
// vitest drift test) will then hold it in sync.
//
// EVERY emitted `.d.mts` opens with a `GENERATED by ... DO NOT EDIT` banner naming
// its source, applied by `stamp()` in `scripts/gen-declarations.ts`
// (EI-18809220546046680) — without it a generated file is indistinguishable from the
// hand-written declarations this repo used until WI-6396, and an edit made in one is
// silently discarded by the next run. Never hand-edit a banner-carrying file: change
// the JSDoc in the `.mjs` and regenerate. The banner sits BELOW any shebang, because
// TypeScript accepts `#!` only at byte 0 (TS18026).
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    // Emitting this repo's own surface, not typechecking its dependencies.
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    // Node's ambient types must be EXPLICIT here. `skipLibCheck` skips .d.ts files,
    // but an input's own .ts SOURCES are still checked — so once an input's import
    // graph reaches a cross-package TS module that uses `node:fs` / `node:path`
    // (check-okf-conformance.mjs -> @papercusp/docs-engine), the whole run dies with
    // TS2591 "Cannot find name 'node:fs'" and emits nothing usable. Measured
    // 2026-08-08: identical tsc invocation, exit 1 without `--types node`, exit 0 with.
    // ⚠ It DOES change existing output — 6 of the 24 pre-existing declarations
    // regenerated differently, and that is an IMPROVEMENT, not drift: node's ambient
    // types were not resolving before, so inference had fallen back to `any` in
    // places. Measured diffs, e.g. `resolveSpec(...): any` -> `string | null`,
    // `repoRoot?: any` -> `string | undefined`, `listOnly?: any` -> `boolean |
    // undefined`. Those 6 must be committed alongside this change.
    // If a future input needs another @types package, ADD it to this array —
    // `types` restricts automatic @types inclusion, so an omission fails at emit time.
    "types": ["node"],
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "target": "es2022",
    // `rootDir` and `outDir` are BOTH the repo root, deliberately: that makes each
    // `.d.mts` land beside its own `.mjs` regardless of which directory it lives
    // in, so one config can serve `scripts/` and `packages/` together. Set only
    // `outDir` and tsc infers a "common source directory" and re-appends it,
    // emitting a nested mirror tree (TS5011).
    "rootDir": ".",
    "outDir": "."
  },
  // `files`, NOT `include`. Because `outDir` is `.`, tsc adds it to the implicit
  // `exclude`, and `exclude` filters `include` — together they cancel out to zero
  // inputs (TS18003 "No inputs were found"). `exclude` does not apply to `files`.
  // An explicit list is also the honest surface: a glob would silently start
  // emitting declarations for every future script in the repo.
  "files": [
    // EI-25217214806027261 — bundle-host's free-reference guard, imported directly by
    // scripts/check-bundle-free-refs.test.ts (the list's first reason: no TS7016).
    "scripts/check-bundle-free-refs.mjs",
    // EI-24834079439388393: ptool's SDK-install race regression imports the
    // maintained mutex and install boundary directly; keep their types generated.
    "scripts/lib/fs-mutex.mjs",
